 "type": "control",
 "summary": "Turns each note written to its track into a chord or an arpeggio on a target (peer) machine: 54 chord types, strum and delay modes, note cut, arpeggio modes and an octave spread. It makes no sound itself.",
 "category": "Control",
 "tags": [
  "chords",
  "arpeggio"
 ],
 "use_for": "Turn single notes into chords and arpeggios played on other machines.",
 "quirks": [
  "It is a control machine: nothing is heard until a target machine is chosen and plays the notes it sends; choosing the target is done in the machine's own window and no tool sets it (the same as Pedal Chord).",
  "A chord needs up to six consecutive free tracks on the target, starting at First target track.",
  "Velocity maps from the target's lowest to its highest velocity (raw 0 to 65,534), not to a fixed 0 to 127.",
  "The octave pairs are packed: each value holds two octave shifts, -8 to +7 (raw 136 is both 0).",
  "Custom note offsets are 0 to 47 semitones; raw 48 means off.",
  "Pedal Chord is the repo's own chord and arpeggio machine, with a source and a page.",
  "Closed source (a prebuilt DLL): names come from its own texts, its DLL's type names and the profile, not from code."
